<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ndwandwe Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1780 CE – 1826 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The powerful kingdom of Zwide, chief rival of the early Zulu, whose defeat scattered leaders who founded new states across southern Africa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndwandwe">Ndwandwe</a> were settled around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mkuze-river">Mkhuze</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pongola-river">Pongola</a> rivers in the north of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a>, with ties to the Dlamini of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swazi-kingdom">Swazi Kingdom</a>. Under Langa and especially his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwide">Zwide</a> in the late 18th and early 19th centuries, they expanded through conquest into a major power.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwide">Zwide</a> organised regiments and dominated his neighbours, driving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sobhuza-i">Sobhuza I's</a> people north and killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingiswayo">Dingiswayo</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mthethwa-paramountcy">Mthethwa Paramountcy</a> around 1818. His mother Ntombazi was a powerful figure at court. The struggle with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaka-zulu-king">Shaka</a> produced battles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gqokli-hill">Gqokli Hill</a> and the decisive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndwandwe">Ndwandwe</a> defeat on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mhlatuze-river">Mhlatuze</a> river around 1819.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwide">Zwide</a> moved north and died around 1825; his son Sikhunyana was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaka-zulu-king">Shaka</a> in 1826. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndwandwe">Ndwandwe</a> commanders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soshangane">Soshangane</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwangendaba">Zwangendaba</a> founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gaza">Gaza</a> state and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngoni">Ngoni</a> kingdoms far to the north.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1780 CE – 1826 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.12%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1780 CE – 1826 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Langa, Zwide, Sikhunyana</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Nguni religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>isiZulu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a>, <a href="/countries/eswatini">Eswatini</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ndwandwe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1803&amp;focus=ndwandwe-kingdom" aria-label="Ndwandwe Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5289 3250 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ndwandwe Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5880 3217h0M5822 3471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5609 3506h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5609 3506h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day South Africa. <a href="/atlas?year=1803&amp;focus=ndwandwe-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

